    "assistant_text": "All 6 tests pass now, including `test_exact_payment_settles_invoice`.\n\n**Cause:** `settle` rounded the discount on each line and then summed the rounded values. That gave 9.32 + 35.22 + 61.12 = 105.66, so the total due was 1324.84 instead of the expected 1324.83.\n\n**Fix:**\n- `settle` in `src/ledger/engine.py` still loops over `invoice.items`, as you required. It now adds up each line's unrounded discount and rounds the sum once. The three lines sum to 105.672, which rounds to 105.67, so the total due is 1324.83.\n- I added `exact_discount_for` to `src/ledger/rules.py`. It returns the unrounded discount for a line, in fractional cents.\n- `discount_for` is unchanged, so the half-up rounding test still passes.\n\n**Finance reconciliation:** the per-line unrounded figures are still computed, but the per-line rounded figures no longer exist inside `settle`. If finance needs those rounded values for reconciliation, `rules.discount_for` still produces them. They will no longer add up exactly to the invoice discount, because the rounding now happens once at the end.",
